// KeeleSepp English B2 (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_EN_B2.md), module 1 „Who we are” (en-b2-001…005), stage English B1+.
// Main topic area of the English state exam: inimene ja ühiskond (people and society), secondary: kultuur (culture) —
// identity, generations and how young people in Estonia live. Grammar axis: the tense system reviewed (present simple and
// continuous, present perfect simple vs continuous, 001), narrative tenses with the past perfect simple (002), the past
// perfect continuous (003), question tags reviewed (004). Exam formats met: EL3 (002), ER1 and ER6 (001), ER2 (004), EW1
// (003), ES1 and ES2 (004); 005 is a short diagnostic in the state exam's task types (one or two tasks a part).
// Lesson template v4, design v2 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12–§13). No recurring cast: every text is written
// for KeeleSepp from the facts named in its source line (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_EN_B2.md §8); the people in the stories,
// podcasts and interviews are invented and quote no invented figures. Listening texts are read by the teacher (owner
// 2026-11-03: no English TTS yet). The teacher's key explanations (Russian): module01Key.js.
//   001 AVAS R→S  Generations: the topic opener, an article on what generation labels can and cannot explain.
//   002 LUGU R→W  The day the money changed: a memoir of 20 June 1992 (the kroon), narrative tenses.
//   003 KUUL L→W  Turning points: a podcast, the reminiscence bump, a letter to a museum's family-story project (EW1).
//   004 RÄÄK L→S  Leaving home: the module's article (Eurostat 2023), question tags, the examiner's set (ES2), photos (ES1).
//   005 EKS       Diagnostic: listening, language use, reading, a letter and the speaking part in the exam's form.
