        'You arrived at nine. When you arrived, the music had stopped, the cake had disappeared and the host was crying. You do not know why. Ask B: „What had happened before I came?”', 'You were there from seven. At eight a dog had run into the garden and eaten the cake, and the neighbours had complained about the music. You left at half past eight. Ask A how the evening ended.',
